-- A decision that pins its CLEAN section number (spec §11 W3(a)) and then
-- opens with a SECOND index. `L4.Blawx.Emit.renderRuleText` would write the
-- rule_text line "4. 5. A director is disqualified.", and clean-law 0.0.4 reads
-- that as one section index with an insert index -- `number + insert_index +
-- DOT`, clean/clean.py:53 -- giving eId sec_4_5 while the workspace we name is
-- sec_4_section. Every canvas in the document would then be orphaned: it
-- imports, it stores, and it belongs to no section of the Act. Measured
-- 2026-09-02 with etc/blawx-eid-harness.py before the refusal existed:
-- "clean-law yields ['sec_4_ 5_section'], workspaces are ['sec_4_section']".
--
-- Sub-provision anchoring (Jason Morris's sec_1__para_a_section) is what the
-- author is reaching for here, and it is W3(b) -- still open. So this refuses
-- by name rather than emitting a document that looks fine and is not.

DECLARE Director HAS
    `is bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN

@export 4. 5. A director is disqualified.
GIVEN d IS A Director
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is disqualified` d IF d's `is bankrupt`
